#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/id #uuid "30d54dcc-49a2-5cd0-9eb9-659413ed5c67" :question/math-academy-id "e-9525" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x,$ where $C=C_1 \\cup C_2$ is the path comprising of two line segments, as shown below.\n\n![](images/3d/3d408de0d50e2688aa0b35d8af39b6847cfdf21d5ec583320f0204384304fbc8.png)" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_2$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $x_1$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $x_2 = -3$ and $x_1 = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1 = (-3) - 3 = -6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179594 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179732 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6935944-0acd-5593-aa80-e56f6014c13f" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to Y"}] :question/id #uuid "d799bcde-dbf0-580e-921b-18e56d729ea1" :question/math-academy-id "e-9526" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y,$ where $C$ is the path along the semicircle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(3,0)$ to the point $(-3,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/ca/ca97546ecaf9e37bee53fcc2b0c66962cff67a91ee9b117cc8ac8531efa23efc.png)" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $y_2$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $y_1$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $y_2 = 0$ and $y_1 = 0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1 =  0 - 0 = 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/id #uuid "e1d24f1c-4b7c-5c5e-bf93-7f9e76dffdf2" :question/math-academy-id "e-9527" :question/problem "If $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= 8$ and $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= -2,$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x$ given that $C = C_1\\cup C_2.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C = C_1\\cup C_2$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = -\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = \\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x + \\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-(-2)-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =2-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x = -6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21c8a8d4-87ed-55f6-b189-8fd096ccb0f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257057} {:answer/id #uuid "a6a2197a-32b5-5271-8856-fa61374bf3f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258235} {:answer/id #uuid "cc772a32-8680-5318-bdd6-377106988be6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258552} {:answer/id #uuid "f7eb6e09-f494-51e4-bf3c-00202fb54123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258956} {:answer/id #uuid "fee6c79a-2226-58b8-ab65-e7cd7095f370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fee6c79a-2226-58b8-ab65-e7cd7095f370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259020} :answer-field/id #uuid "743c3eab-b9ff-5a18-a140-2fb699e08d1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2ecd409-704d-58f0-912b-02eaced8c539" :question/math-academy-id "q-124146" :question/problem "![](images/ac/ac639fb08d54d2004aec96708ffd19bc080b028e739075687a84a09158cd4fd2.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a semicircle of radius $2,$ traversed from the point $(2,1)$ to the point $(-2,1),$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=(-2)-2=-4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179732 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6935944-0acd-5593-aa80-e56f6014c13f" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2384c997-1d5d-53b4-a312-5c2ec9c86073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257079} {:answer/id #uuid "6458baf9-7035-53af-916d-1b7d57ec3bfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257663} {:answer/id #uuid "c6df00e4-14bf-5e23-a939-f984f68a0ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258519} {:answer/id #uuid "e3cc3553-89e2-5ace-abc4-1172afe072cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258761} {:answer/id #uuid "e497e2c8-05df-595e-a19c-1ff2ed39c04b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2384c997-1d5d-53b4-a312-5c2ec9c86073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257079} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4304b44-cbb1-57e3-b024-663ea2e2eb70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46935a1e-c060-58a7-ab7d-a527906c3000" :question/math-academy-id "q-124148" :question/problem "![](images/24/2400f92070b4f7d4e0ad0309574b729da86754bc64b6d7a3c508433d1bbc7f76.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment between the points $(4,0)$ to the point $(0,3),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{2}=3$ and ${y}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=3-0=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f5989ee-33da-5aee-80b5-59f4458347c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415633} {:answer/id #uuid "608438d6-dac5-5e73-81f2-28ee2e83a8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415639} {:answer/id #uuid "65d7c98e-321b-597f-b317-1c771751881a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415641} {:answer/id #uuid "ba35a350-5197-53ed-ab93-7811ac616cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415657} {:answer/id #uuid "f61c2696-a894-5f2d-b3e9-6c094b9ebfe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba35a350-5197-53ed-ab93-7811ac616cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415657} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae3b474-71b1-5e53-80d8-8ff83014500b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e3ca1583-0f44-5bd8-a174-1f7bba09e7fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-124150" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=12$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=8,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 12 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 12 & =-8-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 20 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "361078b9-7f47-5625-8fa1-b6318a31d040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257258} {:answer/id #uuid "76cad87a-c60f-52ba-8fa0-029d07047db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257828} {:answer/id #uuid "a977aafa-6ddc-5df1-a245-8ef489e5f716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258261} {:answer/id #uuid "ccbba914-567c-568a-81b9-9dcb9fa35f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258554} {:answer/id #uuid "d412e256-9897-5bf7-9015-79334c069732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a977aafa-6ddc-5df1-a245-8ef489e5f716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258261} :answer-field/id #uuid "69df9cf6-56f8-5091-8393-12c1f47f7bcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "caa68865-4fa8-5716-bcf1-19dd497b3997" :question/math-academy-id "q-124184" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=15$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=10,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 15 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 15 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-10 \\\\ 25 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-25.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259614 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28d5e447-8418-5713-9439-d989ec5b6429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257147} {:answer/id #uuid "361a934d-451b-5e92-92f4-46a6a1e2211a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257259} {:answer/id #uuid "dc5e7fd0-81d0-5309-8978-db5e8c201730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258701} {:answer/id #uuid "e9498204-facb-59b8-b6f0-bc76230762a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258805} {:answer/id #uuid "f3c4005f-481d-5307-83cd-ce0861f8586f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9498204-facb-59b8-b6f0-bc76230762a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258805} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a217e9-fa91-5a9c-b987-36a79f55e03e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7673d1a0-afd2-5d22-93cd-75c43bd54a25" :question/math-academy-id "q-124186" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=16$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=11,$ calculate ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -16 & =-11+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -5 & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01e4d0b1-3d49-5ae5-b65b-8dbe801177f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415622} {:answer/id #uuid "2a14506d-1bc5-538f-8601-a75415c5af4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415629} {:answer/id #uuid "328548aa-6ec4-5ded-abca-468351c78e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415634} {:answer/id #uuid "53d99d5e-8f7a-5890-a03d-e22ee095b634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415638} {:answer/id #uuid "7b192eed-e4b2-5e18-b229-5a2f13c347d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01e4d0b1-3d49-5ae5-b65b-8dbe801177f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415622} :answer-field/id #uuid "45a9fe64-c73b-5f9f-af73-48b5821ab772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "28b25a72-e404-5d69-993b-a9b2c8d9ba39" :question/math-academy-id "q-124187" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=17,$ ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=7,$ and ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=5,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 17 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+5-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 17 & =-7+5-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 19 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-19.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259615 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51f2bc34-8a89-5463-8fed-40f8b3ee4021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257479} {:answer/id #uuid "6a69ee73-ac87-5840-b9e1-8ab3617e7244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257722} {:answer/id #uuid "6c449e4e-c72b-5c65-9e7c-6c13bdd64261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257736} {:answer/id #uuid "c04eb81a-1440-5aaf-bf1f-87f807655d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258462} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a368c6-a24f-58c9-a5e3-12fe7a102a44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a69ee73-ac87-5840-b9e1-8ab3617e7244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257722} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d1439db-d14d-58d1-a5c6-a4a3380d0598" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8ad1a2a8-0a25-5345-b64f-001fe66a3826" :question/math-academy-id "q-124188" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=21,$ ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=2,$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-11,$ calculate ${\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & =2-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -21 & =2-(-11)+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -21 & =13+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -34 & ={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-34.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18b46eaa-8958-53b6-8687-3a9f1e7e95dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415626} {:answer/id #uuid "69547d52-da29-51bf-acae-befe4ab3ec6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415642} {:answer/id #uuid "8f3d2128-0a37-5623-9bd3-50d58517585b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415650} {:answer/id #uuid "928dd7bb-83bc-5472-82e3-9788fdbdebd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415651} {:answer/id #uuid "d91dbfa3-7b7e-59a5-96a6-b0844635cb03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18b46eaa-8958-53b6-8687-3a9f1e7e95dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415626} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c00917f-f531-55fd-88ca-7ff2a9809cae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81ff799c-e275-561c-accd-b7005d2a330b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124290" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d1c20f44c7a092275f200737813e11c762e1f3e80ba22ded29b41731e22472e.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is the path comprising of two line segments, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=4-0=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105bce54-4026-504a-aebc-d3aeaf976b6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415624} {:answer/id #uuid "2e06e035-45fa-5e53-bfbc-65514f433cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415632} {:answer/id #uuid "c08436b7-7d2d-5354-b7f9-73e0c58fe847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415658} {:answer/id #uuid "dafff622-d36c-559c-aa25-3ffc0e5c93a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415662} {:answer/id #uuid "e3917919-8158-59b4-b944-e19f2eb5c017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e06e035-45fa-5e53-bfbc-65514f433cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415632} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c4667bc-8f59-530d-9f0d-9e00044a377f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4b4530c-a5d4-5bda-8a1d-c3d8365018f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-124306" :question/problem "![](images/05/05b76357203cf2d7ef38b4bfa8daa9e0ce21b248f150e1a2d516f1a4c4e5bef3.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a quarter circle of radius $1,$ traversed from the point $(0,2)$ to the point $(1,1),$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=1-0=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426488 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10710cf3-2461-52e0-8591-26504aac5b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426476} {:answer/id #uuid "268e558d-6b3a-5fd2-8942-b57b576a8436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426478} {:answer/id #uuid "2abac835-c02a-57a9-ab86-5e5d2da016b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426479} {:answer/id #uuid "40b22bf4-a6c7-569e-8fd1-56a445471c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426480} {:answer/id #uuid "70a9bb49-2c55-5047-8c58-bf5ec89dd003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70a9bb49-2c55-5047-8c58-bf5ec89dd003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426481} :answer-field/id #uuid "00fb8aa7-71b4-5be7-ac8f-e5b17414c65f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "15dd7515-4c6a-53a1-ac3c-ffc4846bc122" :question/math-academy-id "q-124328" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d4d60c547afdb873c30e6c5e1f70d616dc31ace79b482f37ae51ea4f036d5a42.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the closed path along the quarter circle of \nradius $2,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17e8204a-f6c5-582c-9a70-1391bf4c46e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415625} {:answer/id #uuid "21124427-bf82-58d2-a56e-34687e5df13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415627} {:answer/id #uuid "3686abdb-2eb3-5b8d-95fd-3506ce16b7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415635} {:answer/id #uuid "b96c24b7-dfe8-55e1-bbe2-db59a4ed77de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/