swer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257282} {:answer/id #uuid "4ebd7418-3bb9-570d-924c-3dc7e9776f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257456} {:answer/id #uuid "9f53e24b-ebea-54a9-8514-7175425da79a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14a3e13b-f507-5f24-bba7-9b2e8578076a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256969} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3a7546e-e56f-5a1a-b125-8d0831f6c296" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c941258b-2cc1-58e8-aec4-791b92e6f425" :question/math-academy-id "q-124341" :question/problem "![](images/1c/1c074157bb6374a4da01d6c1312bb60520966317b1f903eb44a191384e398ae6.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is the path comprising of a quarter circle of radius $3$ and a line segment, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{1}=1$ and ${y}_{2}=-4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=(-4)-1=-5.\n$$"}]}
